From 0000000000000000000000000000000000000000 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: chilogen <chilogen@users.noreply.github.com>
Date: Thu, 29 Oct 2026 16:45:27 +0100
Subject: [PATCH] nvidia-modeset: restore DSC and audio on a DP device that
 reappears

A DSC monitor that resets itself after waking (long HPD, DPCD back at
defaults) comes back as the same device while its head is still driven, so
the stream resumes without a modeset. Two pieces of state that only a modeset
programs were not restored: the sink's DSC decompression enable (DPCD 0x160),
so the sink gets a compressed stream it can't decode and stays black, and the
source audio stream, which stays muted.

Restore DSC where the device rejoins its still driven stream
(processNewDevice() when it was left in its group, GroupImpl::insert() when
the client adds it back), restarting an SST stream so the sink sees it begin
with decompression enabled, and re-run the audio part of a modeset in
notifyZombieStateChange().

From https://github.com/chilogen/dp-dsc-wake-fix (MIT), patches/615.78.08.patch.

Fixes upstream issue 1487; also covers the DSC half of upstream issue 1405
that 615.78.08's dpPreModeset() change doesn't.

Co-Authored-By: Claude Opus 5.5 <noreply@anthropic.com>
